MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Documents the branch's total drift (2 lines + this file), why harness
scripts and vendored packages are deliberately absent (the abgen pipeline
auto-installs its editor scripts; all deps are obtainable), the exact list
of the 8 UPM packages served by the private unity-explorer-packages repo,
and the access options (ssh org key / https+PAT insteadOf / local-mirror
insteadOf for CI rigs — git config hints only, never manifest edits).

---
 docs/ABGEN-COMPARE.md | 91 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 91 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 docs/ABGEN-COMPARE.md

diff --git a/docs/ABGEN-COMPARE.md b/docs/ABGEN-COMPARE.md
new file mode 100644
index 000000000..e887afb88
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/ABGEN-COMPARE.md
@@ -0,0 +1,91 @@
+# abgen-compare — minimal-drift host project for the AB render-parity harness
+
+This branch makes an upstream `decentraland/unity-explorer` checkout usable as
+the **host project** for the abgen render-comparison harness (asset-bundle
+parity vs `ab-cdn.decentraland.org`): the harness renders both sides of every
+bundle pair inside the real client's URP/shader environment, so pixel verdicts
+answer "does it look right *in the client*".
+
+Tested against upstream `dev` @ `94365208b356287656b74f59a1905de5c135f716`
+(2026-07-03). Any later `dev` commit is expected to work; re-verify after big
+package-manifest changes.
+
+## Total drift vs upstream: 2 changed lines + this file
+
+| Change | Why |
+|---|---|
+| `Explorer/Packages/manifest.json` (1 line): `com.decentraland.unity-shared-dependencies` `git@github.com:…` → `https://github.com/…` | the repo is **public**; the https form resolves with plain anonymous git, so opening the project does not require an ssh key for it. Every other public git dependency in the manifest already uses https. |
+| `Explorer/Packages/packages-lock.json` (1 line): same URL rewrite | keeps the lock consistent with the manifest so UPM keeps the pinned hash instead of re-resolving. |
+| `docs/ABGEN-COMPARE.md` (this file) | purpose + requirements documentation. |
+
+Nothing else. Deliberately **not** in this branch:
+
+- **No harness scripts.** The abgen pipeline auto-installs its Unity editor
+  scripts (`AbVisualCompare.cs`, `AbAnimCapture.cs`, `AbProjectSetup.cs`) into
+  `Explorer/Assets/Editor/` at render time, marker-headers keep them fresh
+  (`pipeline/abgencompare/render.py` → `harness_contract.ensure_scripts`).
+  Shipping copies here would only drift.
+- **No vendored packages.** Every dependency is obtainable: public ones over
+  anonymous https, private ones with normal Decentraland org access (below).
+- **No settings/asset edits.** The project's own URP + linear color space
+  configuration is exactly what the harness wants (`AbProjectSetup` is skipped
+  in unity-explorer mode).
+
+## Requirements to open the project
+
+1. **Unity 6000.4.0f1** (see `Explorer/ProjectSettings/ProjectVersion.txt`);
+   any 6000.4.x imports with a migration warning. Batchmode needs an activated
+   license, renders need a real GPU (never `-nographics`).
+2. **git on PATH** — UPM resolves several git-URL packages.
+3. **Access to the private `decentraland/unity-explorer-packages` repo** — see
+   next section. Everything else is anonymous https.
+
+## The private dependency: `decentraland/unity-explorer-packages`
+
+Eight UPM packages resolve from this **private** repo (ssh URLs in the
+manifest, unchanged from upstream):
+
+| Package | `?path=` in the repo |
+|---|---|
+| `com.dcl.gpui-assets` | `/GPUInstancerPro/com.dcl.gpui-assets` |
+| `com.gurbu.gpui-pro` | `/GPUInstancerPro/com.gurbu.gpui-pro` |
+| `com.gurbu.gpui-pro.terrain` | `/GPUInstancerPro/com.gurbu.gpui-pro.terrain` |
+| `com.decentraland.filebrowserpro` | `/FileBrowserPro` |
+| `com.renderheads.avpro.video-ultra` | `/AVProVideo` |
+| `decentraland.grassshader` | `/StylizedGrassShader` |
+| `decentraland.renderfeatures` | `/RenderGraphs/RenderFeatures` |
+| `superscrollview` | `/SuperScrollView` |
+
+A Decentraland engineer needs org access to it, one of:
+
+- **ssh (works as-is):** an ssh key authorized for the org — the manifest's
+  `git@github.com:` URLs resolve directly.
+- **https + PAT:** a personal access token with `repo` read scope, plus a
+  one-time rewrite so UPM's git calls use it (git config, *not* a manifest
+  edit):
+
+  ```bash
+  git config --global url."https://github.com/decentraland/unity-explorer-packages.git".insteadOf \
+      git@github.com:decentraland/unity-explorer-packages.git
+  # then let a credential helper supply the PAT for github.com
+  ```
+
+- **local mirror (offline/CI rigs):** point the same `insteadOf` at a local
+  clone path instead of the https URL. Use a throwaway `GIT_CONFIG_GLOBAL`
+  file exported around the Unity invocation so the rewrite never leaks into
+  the user's real git config. **Trap:** `GIT_CONFIG_GLOBAL` *replaces* the
+  real global config, which is usually where `git lfs install` put the
+  `[filter "lfs"]` block — copy that block into the throwaway file, or UPM
+  checks out LFS-tracked package binaries (e.g. `client-sdk-unity`'s
+  `Google.Protobuf.dll` / `livekit_ffi` natives) as 131-byte pointer files
+  and the project fails compile with `Google.Protobuf` CS0234 errors. This
+  is how the abgen verification rig runs; a real engineer should prefer org
+  access.
+
+## Running the harness
+
+Point the abgen pipeline at this checkout's `Explorer/` directory
+(`abgen-compare config set unity_project /path/to/checkout/Explorer`); it
+detects the `unity-explorer` project mode (client-faithful) and records it in
+each run's provenance. First import is large (tens of minutes, once). Full
+contract: `harness/README.md` in the abgen repo.
-- 
